# What NOT to send to Docker when building the frontend image.
#
# The build context is this folder, and `docker build` uploads all of it to the
# Docker daemon before the first instruction runs. Without this file that is
# 227MB and 15,481 files, to compile about 990KB of actual input.
#
# Speed is the least important reason. The other two matter more.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# node_modules — excluded for CORRECTNESS, not size
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# It holds compiled binaries for the platform it was installed on:
#     @rollup/rollup-win32-x64-msvc
#     @esbuild/win32-x64
# The image is Linux. Copying Windows binaries in makes the build fail with
# "Cannot find module @rollup/rollup-linux-x64-gnu", which reads like a broken
# dependency and is actually a Dockerfile mistake.
#
# The image runs `npm ci` itself, from package-lock.json, so it installs the
# correct Linux binaries. Never ship build artifacts into an image; regenerate
# them there.
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output — rebuilt inside the image
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Your local dist/ is whatever you last built by hand, with whatever env vars
# happened to be set. The image builds its own. Excluding it makes that
# impossible to get wrong.
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — a file copied into a layer stays in that layer forever
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deleting it in a later instruction only hides it; `docker history` still has
# it. Keep it out of the context in the first place.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed to build the bundle
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Playwright specs run in CI against a live app, never during an image build.
e2e/
playwright.config.ts
test-results/
playwright-report/
coverage/

# Excluded so that editing a note does not invalidate the COPY layer and force
# a full rebuild.
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
